{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562343-is-the-presence-of-kindred-not-that-weak-in-middle-kingdom-in-fact","id":1562343,"title":"Is the presence of Kindred not that weak in Middle Kingdom, in fact?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-30T11:06:42-07:00","id":1562343,"title":"Is the presence of Kindred not that weak in Middle Kingdom, in fact?","content":"Mainly for Lasombra Revised<br /> <br /> Most books (mainly KotE ones) tend to describe Far East as a \u201cforbidden zone\u201d for Kindred, most Kindreds there are very rare and scattered, mainly dwell in border or westernized metropolis, even until now (Meixiu in V20 Children of Revolution, it has been 15 yrs though)<br /> <br /> But stuff in Lasombra Revised seems to contradict this? It does acknowledged how hard they make home there, but most stuff there, including the whole concept of \u201cFar East Lasombra\u201d and even \u201cnative Chinese Sabbat\u201d, is almost* never mentioned again, even in KotE books? Normally Wan Kuei must have some impression of them anyway (look at Wu Zao and Anda, especially Wu Zao, they\u2019re already hermits!), I really don\u2019t think you can hide in the rivals\u2019 shadow thousands of year and get no attention from them, no matter how cautious u are, of course tolerance from them is another matter<br /> <br /> It also says ancient Chinese Lasombra exercises power play in the mortal courts and half of them have no direct contact with Wan Kuei, this also seems no sense if you consider how numerous Wan Kuei are in the Middle Kingdom.<br /> <br /> This book\u2019s author Bruce Baugh also writes several KotE books, so there is no room for authors\u2019 difference. I make several guess:<br /> <br /> 1) Wan Kuei really don\u2019t know them (Well I disagree, for all I have typed)<br /> <br /> 2) This Lasombra simply boasts, his clan is always few in the Far East, I guess the whole brood may be only dozens? The so-called Chinese Sabbat maybe just their self-amusement<br /> <br /> 3) Bruce forgot what he wrote before (Emmm)<br /> <br /> And this stuff also contradicts itself, it mentions a Japanese Lasombra lineage, later says few Lasombra in Japan<br /> <br /> Of course I agree many clans may have tried to make resides in Far East in ancient times, but finally failed and forgotten, like it says Brujah and Malkavian used to establish broods in Korea during 1100 BC<br /> <br /> * State of Grace mentions a chinese-Sabbat-built faction called the Diamond Thunderbolt, but that\u2019s all, and I really wonder the what\u2019s the \u201cBeijing\u2019s sorely challenged but ever-growing Sabbat population\u201d. This stuff seems forgetting Wan Kuei at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T12:23:36-07:00","id":1562346,"title":"","content":"I think you're first conflating some things or taking them <i>in extremis</i>. There's a difference between few and nonexistent.<br /> <br /> Did KotE ever said there are no Kindred in the Middle Kingdom? <i>At all</i>? Did this Lasombra said the clan is <i>numerous</i> there? Is said there that the Japanese lineage is <i>big</i>?<br /> <br /> If the answer is no, they are not contradictions. To have influence in the mortal court you need only one vampire, especially if old. To have a lineage I'd say 3 are enough, this already show the line is stable, and they don't even need to be all alive. A single vampire that's the last of their lineage still means the lineage is extant.<br /> <br /> Not having contact is doable in many ways, it doesn't imply not being known. And even if it does, there's also many ways to hide for that long time, as most supernaturals can be pretty hard for others to find and identify when they're not wandering the streets.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I don't see a contradiction or reason for this to be referenced in KotE books to begin with. But there are other two important things to consider:<br /> <br /> First: the setting was still being developed for Asia. KotE was relatively short lived and thus missed a lot on being fleshed out, especially as it missed important phases in the evolution of the setting.<br /> <br /> It's very likely that the absence of Kindred in Asia either wasn't meant to be as rigid as first thought, or was being revised like so many early concepts and first drafts.<br /> <br /> Second: KotE is also written in-character. Do not jump too soon to the conclusion that the narrator of KotE is trustworthy or informed enough. They may have several reasons both to deceive and to have bias in their perception.<br /> <br /> Particularly it was by then already hinted that the Kuei-Jin narrating the books were greatly overemphasizing the narrative of a specific Court, attributing to the whole &quot;Middle Kingdom&quot; what was actually mostly the party line in southeast China.<br /> <br /> So, even if you think there are contradictions, it isn't necessarily the Lasombra Revised that's wrong. It's possibly a deliberate development of the setting by the author beyond what was previously established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T13:14:08-07:00","id":1562347,"title":"","content":"In 5th it's very likely it's nothing but kindred so as off 5th their's probably load of lasombra there. Revised was probably trying to keep it's options open for asian chronicles to allow a bit of flexibility.<br /> <br /> <br /> I tend to write kindred have a lower population density, usually centered around Indonesia, Malaysia and brunei (ashirra territories) but also Mongolia has loads of Gangrel (anda). Wereas they're rarer in China, Myanmar Korea and Japan which are kuei jin strongholds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T13:46:17-07:00","id":1562349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562343-is-the-presence-of-kindred-not-that-weak-in-middle-kingdom-in-fact?p=1562347#post1562347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 5th it's very likely it's nothing but kindred so as off 5th their's probably load of lasombra there. Revised was probably trying to keep it's options open for asian chronicles to allow a bit of flexibility.<br /> <br /> <br /> I tend to write kindred have a lower population density, usually centered around Indonesia, Malaysia and brunei (ashirra territories) but also Mongolia has loads of Gangrel (anda). Wereas they're rarer in China, Myanmar Korea and Japan which are kuei jin strongholds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ignore 5th Ed for this.<br /> <br /> But what I've been thinking about now is something else.<br /> <br /> How numerous are the Kuei-Jin, really? I mean, how many people even manage to climb out of one of the Thousand Hells to begin with? How many ever get to start a Dharma and how many are lost to attrition?<br /> <br /> Are they really that numerous to begin with? Do they need to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T14:59:18-07:00","id":1562352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562343-is-the-presence-of-kindred-not-that-weak-in-middle-kingdom-in-fact?p=1562349#post1562349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ignore 5th Ed for this.<br /> <br /> But what I've been thinking about now is something else.<br /> <br /> How numerous are the Kuei-Jin, really? I mean, how many people even manage to climb out of one of the Thousand Hells to begin with? How many ever get to start a Dharma and how many are lost to attrition?<br /> <br /> Are they really that numerous to begin with? Do they need to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but I figured i'd comment for completion<br /> <br /> I'd say quite numerous in their home turfs, they seem more robust then kindred so I'm assuming the slower creation rate is countered by them being less likely to 'die'. <br /> <br /> I tend to run Kuei-Jin as linked with the dharmic/folklore religions rather than specifically with Asia, which allows me to have them more spread out. For example their are western Kuei-Jin in europe and American due to the spread of Dharmic religions and new age cults which create negative dharma related to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T15:35:53-07:00","id":1562355,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the idea at the time was that you have assorted handfuls of Kindred scattered about Asia in various enclaves, but that the Kuei-jin tend to ignore them because their much more focused on their own internal conflicts or problems with other more numerous supernaturals like the Beast Courts or the Yellow Springs. Sort of the same way you have certain shapeshifters who aren't really involved with the Beast Courts (a lot of Mongolian Silent Striders or Uktena, for example) or Fey who don't interact with the Hsein (the one Troll character in World of Darkness: Tokyo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T03:59:24-07:00","id":1562365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562343-is-the-presence-of-kindred-not-that-weak-in-middle-kingdom-in-fact#post1562343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mainly for Lasombra Revised<br /> <br /> Most books (mainly KotE ones) tend to describe Far East as a \u201cforbidden zone\u201d for Kindred, most Kindreds there are very rare and scattered, mainly dwell in border or westernized metropolis, even until now (Meixiu in V20 Children of Revolution, it has been 15 yrs though)<br /> <br /> But stuff in Lasombra Revised seems to contradict this? It does acknowledged how hard they make home there, but most stuff there, including the whole concept of \u201cFar East Lasombra\u201d and even \u201cnative Chinese Sabbat\u201d, is almost* never mentioned again, even in KotE books? Normally Wan Kuei must have some impression of them anyway (look at Wu Zao and Anda, especially Wu Zao, they\u2019re already hermits!), I really don\u2019t think you can hide in the rivals\u2019 shadow thousands of year and get no attention from them, no matter how cautious u are, of course tolerance from them is another matter<br /> <br /> It also says ancient Chinese Lasombra exercises power play in the mortal courts and half of them have no direct contact with Wan Kuei, this also seems no sense if you consider how numerous Wan Kuei are in the Middle Kingdom.<br /> <br /> This book\u2019s author Bruce Baugh also writes several KotE books, so there is no room for authors\u2019 difference. I make several guess:<br /> <br /> 1) Wan Kuei really don\u2019t know them (Well I disagree, for all I have typed)<br /> <br /> 2) This Lasombra simply boasts, his clan is always few in the Far East, I guess the whole brood may be only dozens? The so-called Chinese Sabbat maybe just their self-amusement<br /> <br /> 3) Bruce forgot what he wrote before (Emmm)<br /> <br /> And this stuff also contradicts itself, it mentions a Japanese Lasombra lineage, later says few Lasombra in Japan<br /> <br /> Of course I agree many clans may have tried to make resides in Far East in ancient times, but finally failed and forgotten, like it says Brujah and Malkavian used to establish broods in Korea during 1100 BC<br /> <br /> * State of Grace mentions a chinese-Sabbat-built faction called the Diamond Thunderbolt, but that\u2019s all, and I really wonder the what\u2019s the \u201cBeijing\u2019s sorely challenged but ever-growing Sabbat population\u201d. This stuff seems forgetting Wan Kuei at all</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the thing with evolving universes, you throw ideas at the wall and some of them do not stick so you ignore them, adjust them or retcon wholly. If we got a proper continuation of the metaplot there would be probably more info on Kindred in Asia but since V20 did not doo that much metaplot progression and Paradox ignores Wan-kuei altogether then most people think that there are no Kindred in Asia and it's impossible to play Cainites in China or Japan because the books say so. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}